<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n26327" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Lĕsūra</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Lĕsōra</span></b> ,
			<i><span class="en">Sid. Carm. 24, 44</span></i>), ae,
			m.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A mountain in Gaul that produced excellent
			cheese</i>, now <i>La Lozère</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 11,
				42, 97, § 240</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Lĕsŭra</span></b> ,
				<i>a small river in Belgium, that runs into the
				Moselle</i>, <i><span class="en">Aus. Mosell.
		365</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
